[2026-01-30T17:02:14.185Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01MK71J6LnNWk64qpKb1UEqW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Semantic Color System Implementation Complete\n\nI've created a comprehensive semantic color system that defines what colors MEAN in the research context. Here's a summary:\n\n### Created Files\n\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/components/report/shared/semanticColors.ts` | Core semantic color definitions and utilities |\n| `src/components/report/shared/SemanticColorContext.tsx` | React context and hooks |\n\n### Semantic Intents\n\nThe system defines 27 semantic intents organized into categories:\n\n**Confidence/Quality:**\n- `highConfidence`, `mediumConfidence`, `lowConfidence` (emerald → amber → red)\n- `highCredibility`, `mediumCredibility`, `lowCredibility`\n\n**Analysis:**\n- `contradiction` (rose) - Conflicting information\n- `gap` (violet) - Missing information\n- `pattern` (cyan) - Detected patterns\n- `causalLink` (blue) - Cause-effect relationships\n\n**Entities:**\n- `person`, `organization`, `location`, `event`, `concept`\n\n**Findings:**\n- `fact`, `claim`, `evidence`, `hypothesis`\n\n**Status:**\n- `active`, `complete`, `paused`, `failed`\n\n**Priority:**\n- `urgent`, `normal`, `deferred`\n\n**Generic:**\n- `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `info`, `neutral`, `muted`, `accent`\n\n### Key Features\n\n1. **Semantic Intent Resolution:** Convert data values to intents:\n   - `scoreToConfidenceIntent(0.85)` → `'highConfidence'`\n   - `priorityToIntent('high')` → `'urgent'`\n   - `statusToIntent('active')` → `'active'`\n\n2. **Theme-Aware Colors:** Each intent maps to both swiss (light) and radar (dark) themes automatically.\n\n3. **React Hooks:**\n   - `useSemanticColors()` - Main hook with all color functions\n   - `useConfidenceColors(score)` - Shorthand for confidence coloring\n   - `useCredibilityColors(score)` - Shorthand for credibility coloring\n   - `usePriorityColors(priority)` - Shorthand for priority coloring\n\n4. **Backwards Compatibility:** `legacyColorToIntent()` maps old color props to semantic intents.\n\n### Usage Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction ConfidenceIndicator({ score }: { score: number }) {\n  const { forConfidence, badgeClasses } = useSemanticColors();\n  const colors = forConfidence(score);\n\n  return (\n    <span className={`${colors.bg} ${colors.text} ${colors.border} border rounded px-2`}>\n      {Math.round(score * 100)}%\n    </span>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThis ensures \"high confidence\" always means emerald/green across all components, while \"contradiction\" always means rose/red, providing visual consistency throughout the application."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_read_input_tokens":152643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb700aba-f9fc-4283-93cf-561e37220b63","uuid":"d755198c-eb3d-4256-b3b0-6c98a3edb6be"}
